From 98f93e670ad27a64ef0adac145a4c92e5003dc1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xander Burchartz <210020462+xanderburchartz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:50:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 04/32] s52plib: draw arcs (CARC) through the DC path when
 drawing to a DC

RenderCARC chooses RenderCARC_GLSL whenever m_useGLSL is set. m_useGLSL is
set by SetGLOptions and never cleared, but RenderCARC_GLSL only draws with
GL and has no wxDC branch. When the chart is drawn to a DC (m_pdc set)
after GL was enabled, arcs such as light sectors do not end up on the
DC. Use the GLSL path only when there is no DC.

Same change as OpenCPN pull request #5555.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libs/s52plib/src/s52plib.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libs/s52plib/src/s52plib.cpp b/libs/s52plib/src/s52plib.cpp
index 7bbfdb532..5c29265b7 100644
--- a/libs/s52plib/src/s52plib.cpp
+++ b/libs/s52plib/src/s52plib.cpp
@@ -7098,7 +7098,9 @@ int s52plib::RenderMPS(ObjRazRules *rzRules, Rules *rules) {
 
 int s52plib::RenderCARC(ObjRazRules *rzRules, Rules *rules) {
 #ifdef ocpnUSE_GL
-  if (m_useGLSL)
+  // m_useGLSL stays true once the GL options were set, also when drawing to a
+  // wxDC; RenderCARC_GLSL has no DC branch.
+  if (m_useGLSL && !m_pdc)
     return RenderCARC_GLSL(rzRules, rules);
   else
 #endif
